{
  "$comment": [
    "SB-214 / DoD-19 baseline for the settings bar.",
    "",
    "Captured from the pristine monkeytype reference checkout, from",
    "frontend/src/ts/components/pages/test/TestConfig.tsx (the `variables`,",
    "`buttonClass` and `cardClass` declarations and the three pill wrappers) and",
    "frontend/src/styles/tailwind.css (the --breakpoint-* scale). Default theme",
    "serika_dark; the theme contributes only --roundness, which both trees read",
    "through the same `rounded-(--roundness)` utility.",
    "",
    "DoD-19 says the SB-214 diff measures GEOMETRY, not content: card radii,",
    "gaps, paddings and font sizes (SB-081-083), with label text and icons masked",
    "out of the comparison region. In this tree those four quantities are fully",
    "determined by the declarations recorded below, so the comparison is done",
    "against them rather than against a PNG. That makes the check deterministic,",
    "browser-free and CI-runnable, and it fails on exactly the changes a pixel",
    "diff would catch. What it does NOT cover is a rendered-pixel regression that",
    "leaves every declaration intact (a global reset change, a font-metric",
    "change). See __screenshots__/README.md.",
    "",
    "REGENERATE ONLY BY AN EXPLICIT, REVIEWED COMMIT (DoD-19)."
  ],

  "source": {
    "repo": "monkeytype",
    "files": [
      "frontend/src/ts/components/pages/test/TestConfig.tsx",
      "frontend/src/styles/tailwind.css"
    ],
    "theme": "serika_dark"
  },

  "breakpoints": {
    "md": 849,
    "lg": 1105,
    "xl": 1361,
    "2xl": 1617
  },

  "//": "The SB-214 widths are exactly monkeytype's md/lg/xl/2xl thresholds, so these four samples cover every responsive branch the bar has.",
  "sampleWidths": [849, 1105, 1361, 1617],

  "declaredVariables": {
    "base": {
      "--card-gap": "0.25em",
      "--font-size": "0.5em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "0.4em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.5rem"
    },
    "md": {
      "--card-gap": "1em",
      "--font-size": "0.6em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "0.45em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    },
    "lg": {
      "--card-gap": "1em",
      "--font-size": "0.75em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "0.5em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    },
    "xl": {
      "--card-gap": "2em",
      "--font-size": "0.75em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "1em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    }
  },

  "resolved": {
    "849": {
      "--card-gap": "1em",
      "--font-size": "0.6em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "0.45em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    },
    "1105": {
      "--card-gap": "1em",
      "--font-size": "0.75em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "0.5em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    },
    "1361": {
      "--card-gap": "2em",
      "--font-size": "0.75em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "1em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    },
    "1617": {
      "--card-gap": "2em",
      "--font-size": "0.75em",
      "--horizontal-padding": "1em",
      "--vertical-padding": "0.75rem"
    }
  },

  "cardClasses": [
    "card",
    "rounded-(--roundness)",
    "bg-sub-alt",
    "px-(--horizontal-padding)"
  ],

  "controlPaddingClasses": [
    "px-(--horizontal-padding)",
    "py-(--vertical-padding)"
  ],

  "containerClasses": [
    "grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr]",
    "[font-size:var(--font-size)]",
    "mb-8",
    "w-max",
    "place-self-center",
    "justify-center",
    "mx-auto",
    "md:grid",
    "hidden"
  ],

  "cardGapClasses": {
    "left": "mr-(--card-gap)",
    "right": "ml-(--card-gap)"
  }
}
